meta {
  name: Transfer - Reject
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/{{transferId}}/reject
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "rejectionReason": "Leaked tube"
  }
}

tests {
  test("201 Created", function () { expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201); });
}

docs {
  Receiving branch: reject a RECEIVED or ACCEPTED transfer (mandatory reason).

  For an INTERNAL transfer the test goes back to the sender in the same transaction
  (reason recorded on the history):
  - from RECEIVED: the sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT (its
    report never left the sender);
  - from ACCEPTED: the receiving copy is voided, the report is reset and returns to the
    sender, and the original sample goes to REPEAT. Refused (422 SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED)
    when a report at the receiving branch already has a validated result (Result Done,
    Approved, Published), and refused (422 SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH) when the receiving
    branch has itself passed the copy on to another branch, partner or outsource
    centre - it must retrieve it first.
  The sender's referring panel (B2B) is notified once the change has committed.
  The reason is mandatory: `rejectionReason` must contain at least one non-space character
  (max 255). Missing, empty, spaces-only, invisible-characters-only (zero-width space etc.) or non-text values are refused with 400
  VALIDATION_ERROR and nothing changes. The same applies to the group call.
  Who may act (INTERNAL transfer): only the RECEIVING branch. The caller's active
  branch (the profile they switched to) must be the transfer's destination, otherwise
  403 TRANSFER_WRONG_BRANCH and nothing changes. The same applies to pick-up, receive
  and accept. A caller with no active branch (business admin) is refused too. A group
  action is refused as a whole, never skipped, when any transfer belongs to another
  branch.
  Internal branch transfer rules:
  - Once a sample is SENT_INTERNAL to another branch, the SENDER still sees its
    report in the Technician worklist but it is VIEW-ONLY: every write is refused with
    409 LAB_REPORT_SENT_OUT until the transfer is received or returned.
  - A sent sample accepts ONLY Retrieve from the sender, and only until the
    receiving branch has received it (transfer IN_TRANSIT / PICKED_UP).
  - The receiving branch's Reject / Repeat returns the test to the sender: the
    sender's original sample goes SENT_INTERNAL -> REPEAT automatically.

  Group actions with `skipInvalid: true` (bulk Reject / Repeat): a transfer that cannot
  go back is SKIPPED, listed in `skipped` with its reason, and the others still go
  through. Each send-back runs in its own savepoint, so a skipped transfer leaves
  nothing changed. This covers a validated result at the receiver
  (422 SAMPLE_RETURN_BLOCKED) and a copy that was already passed on
  (422 SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH). Without `skipInvalid` the refusal is raised as an error.

  **Sent – Repeated / Sent – Rejected (sender's tube after the receiving branch sends it back).**
  When the receiving branch Repeats or Rejects an INTERNAL transfer (before or after
  Accept), the SENDER's original tube is NOT moved to Repeat any more: it stays
  `SENT_INTERNAL`, its transfer is closed as `REPEAT` / `REJECTED` (with the receiving
  branch's reason), and the sender's list reads "Sent – Repeated" / "Sent – Rejected"
  (the reason is the tooltip; the sender's history also gets a "returned by the
  receiving branch" row, no status change). The report is already reset and back at the
  sender, view-only until the sender decides. The sender then chooses:
    - **Sent – Repeated:** `POST order-samples/:id/repeat` (tube -> Repeat);
    - **Sent – Rejected:** `POST order-samples/:id/error` (tube -> Error, then Repeat).
  Repeat is refused (422 `SAMPLE_SENT_TO_BRANCH`) on a Sent tube whose transfer is still
  open or was rejected, and Error on one whose transfer is open or was repeated - even for a
  forced group call. Only the SENDING branch may do it (403 `TRANSFER_WRONG_BRANCH`),
  like Retrieve. Retrieve itself is REFUSED on a sent-back tube (422 `SAMPLE_RETRIEVE_BLOCKED`: it would only put the tube back to Accepted as if nothing had happened). The sender's Repeat / Error does NOT delete the receiving branch's
  closed transfer; the referring panel is notified at this point (not when the receiving
  branch clicked). On a cancelled order the tube stays frozen: Repeat, Error and Retrieve are all refused.

  **Back on the sender's own copy (Phase 2).** After the existing clear-down (values, notes, attachments and flags removed,
  report back to Pending) and the move back, the report points at the SENDER's Branch Master Data copy of the test again
  (`labTestId`) and `performingBranchLabTestId` is cleared (the order line's entry applies). A panel member's
  `memberBranchLabTestId` returns to the member entry it had. The sender's TAT clock restarts when it accepts the
  tube again. Still allowed only until a report has a validated result (Result Done, Approved, Published).
}
